Build the overlay Windows installer from the build tag

Purpose: a Windows installer of the overlay that students and
colleagues can download from one fixed public URL, and that says in
its About dialog which build it is.

Approach: .github/workflows/overlay-windows-build.yml runs only when
the build tag is pushed (git overlay-build), so a build is a
deliberate act. It reuses upstream's just/MSYS2 installer recipes and
uploads the result under a fixed name to a public prerelease on the
build tag, replacing the previous one. A 'version-extra' meson option
is appended to the version suffix; CI sets it to +overlay-<sha>, and
the release notes list the patch subjects above upstream main.

Constraints: 'just configure' interpolates its arguments unquoted, so
version-extra must stay free of spaces and parentheses. The option
defaults to empty, leaving stock builds unchanged.
